language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ circular_table_averbach_1_2: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Three players (X, Y, Z) of different nationalities (American, English, French) are seated around a circular table playing a game of Hearts. Each passed three cards to the person on their right. Y passed three hearts to the American. X passed the queen of spades and two diamonds to the person who passed their cards to the Frenchwoman. Determine the nationality of each person. The seats are numbered 0, 1, 2 so that 1 is right of 0, 2 is right of 1, and 0 is right of 2; a value denotes the seat, and a player and a nationality with the same value are the same person.
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/circular_table_averbach_1_2.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ x: the seat of player X, 0 to 2
find x : int(0..2)
$ y: the seat of player Y, 0 to 2
find y : int(0..2)
$ z: the seat of player Z, 0 to 2
find z : int(0..2)
$ american: the seat of the American, 0 to 2
find american : int(0..2)
$ english: the seat of the Englishman, 0 to 2
find english : int(0..2)
$ french: the seat of the Frenchwoman, 0 to 2
find french : int(0..2)

such that
$ the three players sit in different seats
allDiff([x, y, z]),
$ the three nationalities are held by different seats
allDiff([american, english, french]),
$ Y passed three hearts to the American, who sits on the right of Y
american = (y + 1) % 3,
$ X passed to the person to the right of X, who is the one who passed to the Frenchwoman, so the Frenchwoman sits on the right of that person
french = (x + 2) % 3
